{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "project-driveschedule-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.62: `project-driveschedule`, a PROJECT-domain run two of whose on-network links carry a USER DRIVE SCHEDULE (driveScheduleSecondLink), computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus its PROJECT input database (`inputs/washtenaw-project-driveschedule.esm`). It selects source types 21 (gasoline) and 62 (diesel), road types 4 and 5, running CO, Total Energy and atmospheric CO2, brake wear and tire wear (PM10 and PM2.5).\n\nWHAT IT EXERCISES: step 100's first arm (java:309-393). LinkOperatingModeDistributionGenerator walks link 1's 110-second signal approach and link 2's 67-second ramp merge second by second -- each second's own grade, the backward differences with 0 for a first second and after link 2's three-second gap, the CASE, the five-decimal quotients -- in place of two bracketing schedules (`lsec_*`, `lsl_*`), and writes each schedule's average speed into Link before ProjectTAG reads it (java:937-948): link 1's SHO and tire-wear mode are at 21.1 mph, not its stated 30, and link 2's at 50.8, not 45 (`run_linkAvgSpeed`). Link 3 beside them on road type 4 brackets as before. Before the port the model refused it (`run_userLinkSchedules` 177, the schedules' rows).\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 3672. `run_domainUnported` is 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "project-domain"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
